ecame unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. It was rolled back in all regions to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback the service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Next steps: find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The errors have stopped.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments.\" The one that was failing is **payments-api**, so that's the one I rolled back. It had been running v5.1.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v5.0.0 is the only earlier release in its history, and it was healthy in production. It's now live in all three regions. The service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%. No approval was needed because v5.0.0 had been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-api), and it paged the on-call engineer. My first attempt timed out. I checked the incident list, found nothing had been created, and retried with the same idempotency key, so there's only one incident.\n\nNext, someone needs to find what's wrong with v5.1.0 before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}